  "body_text": "Pastor John  Adams By admin / July 28, 2025 John Adams is the Pastor of First Baptist Church, Easley since 2001. He has served churches in North Carolina,  Virginia, and Texas. He married the love of his life, Donna, in 1983. They are immensely and incredibly blessed with a son, Joshua and his wife, Alexa. John graduated from Furman University (B.A., 1983) Southeastern Baptist Theological Seminary (M.Div., 1986), and Baylor University (Ph.D., 1994). His academic pursuit has been to understand the variegated movement of evangelicalism in America. He not only studies evangelical movement in America (and beyond); he lives within this movement every day as a Pastor. He has taught as adjunct faculty at Furman University, Gardner-Webb Divinity School, and, for the last thirteen years, at Anderson University in their Master’s Program in Christian Studies (History of Christianity). His calling is to serve the church as a Pastor and to invite everyone to the banquet table of Jesus Christ.",
  "content_html": "<main class=\"site-main\" id=\"main\">\n<article class=\"post-1691 board_members type-board_members status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry ast-article-single\" id=\"post-1691\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/CreativeWork\">\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\" itemprop=\"headline\">Pastor John  Adams</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\">By <span class=\"posted-by vcard author\" itemprop=\"author\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Person\"> <a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://scupstatefoundation.org/author/admin/\" itemprop=\"url\" rel=\"author\" title=\"View all posts by admin\">\n<span class=\"author-name\" itemprop=\"name\">\n\t\t\t\tadmin\t\t\t</span>\n</a>\n</span>\n\n\t\t / <span class=\"posted-on\"><span class=\"published\" itemprop=\"datePublished\"> July 28, 2025 </span></span></div>\n</header><!-- .entry-header -->\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\">\n<p>John Adams is the Pastor of First Baptist Church, Easley since 2001. He has served churches in North Carolina,  Virginia, and Texas. He married the love of his life, Donna, in 1983. They are immensely and incredibly blessed with a son, Joshua and his wife, Alexa.</p>\n<p>John graduated from Furman University (B.A., 1983) Southeastern Baptist Theological Seminary (M.Div., 1986), and Baylor University (Ph.D., 1994). His academic pursuit has been to understand the variegated movement of<br/>\nevangelicalism in America. He not only studies evangelical movement in America (and beyond); he lives within this movement every day as a Pastor.</p>\n<p>He has taught as adjunct faculty at Furman University, Gardner-Webb Divinity School, and, for the last thirteen years, at Anderson University in their Master’s Program in Christian Studies (History of Christianity).</p>\n<p>His calling is to serve the church as a Pastor and to invite everyone to the banquet table of Jesus Christ.</p>\n</div><!-- .entry-content .clear -->\n</div>\n</article><!-- #post-## -->\n </main>",
